      "message": "Given that we\u0027re already using this macro style, I\u0027m ok with landing this as-is. However, it would be easier to read/maintain/debug if we [avoided macros](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Preprocessor_Macros).\n\n```\nstatic inline void download_from_flash(uint32_t src_offset, uint32_t dest_addr,\n\t\t\t\t       uint32_t size,\n\t\t\t\t       enum API_SIGN_OPTIONS_T sign,\n\t\t\t\t       uint32_t exe_addr,\n\t\t\t\t       enum API_RETURN_STATUS_T *status)\n{\n\t((download_from_flash_ptr)ADDR_DOWNLOAD_FROM_FLASH)(\n\t\tsrc_offset, dest_addr, size, sign, exe_addr, status);\n}\n```\n\nWe can also use a constant for the address:\n\n```\nstatic const volatile uint32_t *ADDR_DOWNLOAD_FROM_FLASH \u003d 0x40;\n```\n\n\nI\u0027ll leave it up to you if you want to change the OTP declarations to functions in this CL and then clean up `download_from_flash` in a separate CL or submit them as macros in this CL and then create a followup CL that changes both `download_from_flash` and `opti_*`.",
